7592186499285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107381 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107381 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107381 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107381 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6dc75e3b-a075-5d84-8499-595f1ab73862" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186498753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108275 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "79a1b12e-9b5e-5cf2-a5c0-09f1566e0c71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110299 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1088" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110299 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\left(x^2y\\right)^3\\cdot x^2y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110299 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee3fd0ee-77a9-5ebb-9bc9-c7439f5946b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110299 #edb/ref 1074 "We start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({x}^{2}y)}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y= &  \\\\ {({x}^{2})}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2\\cdot 3}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y & = \\\\ {x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y= &  \\\\ {x}^{6}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot y= &  \\\\ {x}^{6+2}\\cdot {y}^{3+1} & = \\\\ {x}^{8}\\cdot {y}^{4} & = \\\\ {x}^{8}{y}^{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110300 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110300 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $a=2x^3$ and $b=\\dfrac{x}{y},$ express $ab^2$ in terms of $x$ and $y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110300 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d8aca072-8ed5-5d49-8d4e-8bcc96a27ddb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110300 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we substitute for $a$ and $b\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{b}^{2}=2{x}^{3}{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}=2{x}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply and apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}) & = \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{3+2}}{{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{5}}{{y}^{2}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110301 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110301 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac {\\sqrt{y}} {\\sqrt[3]{y}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110301 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf539049-76f2-56c0-a890-00c2d767c0a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110301 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite the radicals as fractional exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt[3]{y}}=\\frac{{y}^{1/2}}{{y}^{1/3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{1/2}}{{y}^{1/3}} & = \\\\ {y}^{1/2-1/3} & = \\\\ {y}^{3/6-2/6} & = \\\\ {y}^{1/6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we express the result as a radical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/6}=\\sqrt[6]{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110661 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110661 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110661 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110661 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110915 #edb/ref 1