1043 #edb/ref 17592186111595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1045 "Combining the Rules of Exponents With Algebraic Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "7fe1fb12-e10b-5870-8007-02f1eb2f68f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186107381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1069 "q-141978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1071 "${(x{y}^{2})}^{2}\\cdot xy=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a9eb6cb-b287-518f-b5b6-3a57acbb1da3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1074 "We start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x{y}^{2})}^{2}\\cdot xy={x}^{2}\\cdot ({y}^{2})^{2}\\cdot xy & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot ({y}^{2})^{2}\\cdot xy & = \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2\\cdot 2}\\cdot xy & = \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{4}\\cdot xy & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{4}\\cdot xy & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}\\cdot x)\\cdot ({y}^{4}\\cdot y) & = \\\\ {x}^{2+1}\\cdot {y}^{4+1} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{5} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}{y}^{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186108275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{100{x}^{7}{y}^{3}}{20{x}^{3}{y}^{2}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d7c1ad1-12d2-56a0-a936-eae89426f942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1074 "We separate the fraction, group the two variables separately, and apply the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{100{x}^{7}{y}^{3}}{20{x}^{3}{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{100}{20}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{7}}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ 5\\cdot {x}^{(7-3)}\\cdot {y}^{(3-2)} & = \\\\ 5{x}^{4}{y}^{1} & = \\\\ 5{x}^{4}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1061 3561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ff971efe-57b1-5d6a-a9d6-53728830ae56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1061 3562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a787c3de-89d7-50ac-b1ff-50a2fb31a2ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1061 3565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8884d25c-0665-5e4b-b13b-866ef3ec66f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111597 #edb/ref 1061 3569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111597 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "73248b69-f18a-503e-b712-b3f56ae6841a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111597 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1061 37772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d8d59c7e-2b45-5493-a09c-f4211a690c16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1064 "Sometimes, we might need to use more than one rule of exponents to simplify an expression. First, let's remind ourselves of all of the rules of exponents.\n\n- Radicals as fractional exponents: $\\sqrt[n]{x} = x^{1/n}$\n\n- The product rule: $a^n \\cdot a^m = a^{n+m}$\n\n- The quotient rule: $\\dfrac{a^n}{a^m} = a^{n-m}$\n\n- The power rule: $\\left( a^m \\right)^n = a^{mn}$\n\n- The power of product rule: $(ab)^n = a^nb^n$\n\n- The power of quotient rule: $\\left(\\dfrac a b \\right)^n = \\dfrac{a^n}{b^n}$\n\nAs an example, let's simplify the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\left(u^2 v\\right)^3\n$$\n\nWe start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({u}^{2}v)}^{3}={({u}^{2})}^{3}\\cdot {v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({u}^{2})}^{3}\\cdot {v}^{3} & = \\\\ {u}^{(2\\cdot 3)}\\cdot {v}^{3} & = \\\\ {u}^{6}\\cdot {v}^{3} & = \\\\ {u}^{6}{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1065 1485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "13b1c64a-c868-5824-919e-c3a665bb4a96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111904 #edb/ref 1064 "To simplify the expression $x\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{x^2},$ we first rewrite the radical as a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\nx \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{x^2} = x \\cdot \\left( x^2 \\right)^{1/3}\n$$\n\nNow, we apply the power rule for exponents:\n\n$$\nx \\cdot \\left( x^2 \\right)^{1/3} = x \\cdot x^{2(1/3)} = x \\cdot x^{2/3}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {x}^{2/3} & = \\\\ {x}^{1+2/3} & = \\\\ {x}^{5/3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we express the result as a radical:\n\n$$\nx^{5